## Scope

Part 2 fixed the script findings only: F2 (plan half), F1, F3, F4, F5, F6, F11, and F13.
The Red tests in commit d985d325 did not change. Guard G-1 holds: no shared file changed.
No test file changed. `plan.md` is unchanged (the measure-guard rule of the brief).

## Fixes

- F2 plan half: `planQuestBuild` wraps `questLayout` in a try/catch and pushes the reader error.
  The plan then returns an error and writes nothing.
- F1: the new export `questPanelValues` returns errors for a missing or corrupt phonics graph, a
  corrupt week file, a level without week files, a unit without weeks, and an empty panel. `main`
  prints the errors and exits 1 before it makes a folder or writes a file.
- F3: the plan reads each out sub folder with lstat. A symlink gives an error that names the folder.
- F4: the PDF/X step writes into the build temp folder. The build copies the four print files to
  the out folder only after the fourth step passes. A failure leaves no print file in the out folder.
- F5: `artFileBoundaryError` refuses an art file or reader picture that is a symlink and resolves
  outside the pictures folder. The error names the file.
- F6: `artFileBoundaryError` refuses an art file above 64 MB and names the file.
  The test uses 100 MB, so any cap from 30 to 99 MB passes.
- F11: `qrCheck` reads the style of the QR box and compares its width and height with
  `QUEST_BOXES`. A 20 mm box fails.
- F13: `readGitHead` reads `.git/HEAD`, the ref file, or the packed refs, and validates 40 hex
  characters. Each `build-report.json` holds `gitHead`.
  Deviation from the brief: it reads files with `fs` and spawns no process. The committed B12 test
  allows only `process.execPath`, `node`, `pdfinfo`, `pdftotext`, `pdfimages`, and `pdftoppm` as a
  spawn command, so a `git` child process would fail B12. The value equals `git rev-parse HEAD`.
  The ADV-8 test proves this with `git merge-base --is-ancestor`.

## Notes for review

- `questPanelValues` is a new export. It is the only new public function.
- A week file with a schema error now fails the build for the whole level, not only for its unit.
  A broken week file is not trustworthy input for the panel.
- The panel check runs after the plan and before the first `mkdirSync`.

